Helm itself does not create a "helm folder" after installation.

Check Helm Installation
Shell
helm version

Locate Helm binary:

Shell
which helm

Example:

Shell
/usr/local/bin/helm

or

Shell
/usr/bin/helm
Helm Configuration Location

Check Helm environment:

Shell
helm env

Typical directories:

Plain Text
HELM_CACHE_HOME=/root/.cache/helm
HELM_CONFIG_HOME=/root/.config/helm
HELM_DATA_HOME=/root/.local/share/helm

View them:

Shell
ls -la ~/.config/helm
ls -la ~/.cache/helm
ls -la ~/.local/share/helm
Where Helm Stores Repositories
Shell
~/.config/helm/repositories.yaml

View:

Shell
cat ~/.config/helm/repositories.yaml
Where Downloaded Charts Are Stored

If you run:

Shell
helm pull bitnami/nginx

A file appears in your current directory:

Plain Text
nginx-<version>.tgz

After extraction:

Shell
tar -xvf nginx-*.tgz

You'll get:

Plain Text
nginx/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── templates/
└── charts/

This is what many people call the Helm chart folder.

Create Your Own Helm Chart
Shell
helm create myapp

This creates:

Plain Text
myapp/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
├── charts/
└── templates/
├── deployment.yaml
├── service.yaml
└── ingress.yaml

Verify:

Shell
tree myapp

If your goal is to use Helm with ArgoCD, run:

Shell
helm create java-webapp

and you'll get the complete Helm chart folder structure that can be pushed to GitHub and deployed using ArgoCD.

